  "body": "Part of #2574 (research answers 4 and 5).\n\nMaintainer request, 2026-11-18, in his words (quoted in #2574):\n> \"the ability to playback a G-code file in a stand alone Application called camcraft-sim, which opens a g-code file, takes a mch and a cps files as references for making sure it does what it should be doing.\"\n\n## What is missing\nThe travel, feed, rpm, tool count and tool size checks exist only in `app` and read the ECS world: `check_ops(world, ...)` in `crates/app/src/machine/mod.rs` (lines 158-175) and the helpers in `crates/app/src/machine/judge.rs`. A stand-alone `camcraft-sim` cannot call them.\n\n## Scope\n- Move the world-free half (judge a list of moves, tools and rpm against a `Machine`) to `camcraft-post::machine`. Keep `MachineCheck` and `REPORT_CAP` with it.\n- `app` keeps the walk over the operations and calls the moved function. `app` re-exports it.\n- Each finding can carry a source location (an operation name in the app, an NC line number in `camcraft-sim`).\n- The output of the app check does not change. This is under the safety floor: the existing machine-check tests must stay green with no change of their asserts.\n- No new crate edge (`app` already depends on `camcraft-post`).\n\n## Done means\n`camcraft-post` has a pure limit judgment over moves with tests in `crates/post/tests/`. The existing app machine-check tests pass with no change of their asserts.\n",
